1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:03,129
An appeals court agreed that a witness at

2
00:00:03,129 --> 00:00:06,690
Sunny Balwani's fraud trial gave false testimony.

3
00:00:07,116 --> 00:00:09,847
So why does his conviction still stand?

4
00:00:10,183 --> 00:00:14,087
In October, the Supreme Court refused to hear his case.

5
00:00:14,450 --> 00:00:19,207
By the end, you'll see the one sentence that kept his conviction standing.

6
00:00:19,549 --> 00:00:21,533
And there's a second puzzle.

7
00:00:21,883 --> 00:00:25,845
Elizabeth Holmes was acquitted of defrauding patients.

8
00:00:25,845 --> 00:00:27,899
Balwani was convicted of it.

9
00:00:28,249 --> 00:00:31,624
Today you'll learn what he ran, what patients received,

10
00:00:31,624 --> 00:00:34,631
and how two juries reached two different results.

11
00:00:35,149 --> 00:00:36,086
Chapter one.

12
00:00:36,086 --> 00:00:37,256
The number two.

13
00:00:37,256 --> 00:00:40,376
Was Balwani really just Holmes's deputy?

14
00:00:40,883 --> 00:00:44,985
The appeals court says he and Holmes were

15
00:00:44,985 --> 00:00:49,487
in a romantic relationship from 2004 to 2016.

16
00:00:50,083 --> 00:00:53,469
He joined Theranos in 2009 and was later

17
00:00:53,469 --> 00:00:57,870
appointed its president and chief operating officer.

18
00:00:58,450 --> 00:01:03,755
Prosecutors say he worked there from September 2009 to July

19
00:01:03,755 --> 00:01:09,240
2016, as board member, chief operating officer and president.

20
00:01:09,816 --> 00:01:11,000
And he had a stake.

21
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:15,235
Nearly thirty million shares, more than six per cent of the company.

22
00:01:15,750 --> 00:01:20,221
According to the court, he oversaw the patient-testing lab and was

23
00:01:20,221 --> 00:01:24,556
the main contact for the retail partners, Safeway and Walgreens.

24
00:01:25,116 --> 00:01:28,218
The court adds that the exact split of duties

25
00:01:28,218 --> 00:01:31,319
between him and Holmes was disputed at trial.

26
00:01:31,883 --> 00:01:35,121
His own words, shown to his jury, according to

27
00:01:35,121 --> 00:01:38,852
Fortune: I am responsible for everything at Theranos.

28
00:01:39,416 --> 00:01:40,246
Chapter two.

29
00:01:40,246 --> 00:01:40,799
The lab.

30
00:01:40,799 --> 00:01:43,427
What did the man in charge of it know?

31
00:01:43,916 --> 00:01:46,993
Theranos promised fast blood tests from a few

32
00:01:46,993 --> 00:01:49,864
drops, run on its own machine, the Edison.

33
00:01:50,416 --> 00:01:55,092
The court says Theranos developed three hundred small-sample tests.

34
00:01:55,092 --> 00:01:57,883
Only twelve were ever run on the Edison.

35
00:01:58,383 --> 00:02:02,475
For visiting investors, the court says, the device ran a null

36
00:02:02,475 --> 00:02:07,574
protocol, while some samples were secretly run on other companies' machines.

37
00:02:08,150 --> 00:02:11,251
Former employees testified that the Edison

38
00:02:11,251 --> 00:02:14,426
consistently failed quality control checks.

39
00:02:14,426 --> 00:02:18,636
The court says they told Holmes and Balwani in real time.

40
00:02:19,216 --> 00:02:22,584
In a text to Holmes, reported by NBC Bay

41
00:02:22,584 --> 00:02:26,961
Area, Balwani called a Theranos lab a disaster zone.

42
00:02:27,550 --> 00:02:33,118
Associated Press reporting dates that message to 2014.

43
00:02:33,616 --> 00:02:37,802
In late 2015, federal inspectors arrived unannounced.

44
00:02:37,802 --> 00:02:43,174
They found deficiencies posing immediate jeopardy to patient health.

45
00:02:43,683 --> 00:02:47,666
Here is the regulator's letter of March 2016.

46
00:02:47,666 --> 00:02:50,232
Look who it was addressed to.

47
00:02:50,716 --> 00:02:55,912
It proposed revoking the lab's licence, fines of ten thousand dollars a day,

48
00:02:55,912 --> 00:03:00,013
and a ban of at least two years on its owners and operators.

49
00:03:00,583 --> 00:03:03,753
For several deficiencies, Theranos told the

50
00:03:03,753 --> 00:03:06,775
regulator no patient impact was expected.

51
00:03:06,775 --> 00:03:12,157
The agency said it gave no information on how it reached that conclusion.

52
00:03:12,716 --> 00:03:13,648
Chapter three.

53
00:03:13,648 --> 00:03:14,513
The patients.

54
00:03:14,513 --> 00:03:17,175
What happens when a blood test is wrong?

55
00:03:17,683 --> 00:03:20,738
Prosecutors laid it out after sentencing.

56
00:03:20,738 --> 00:03:24,463
A doctor received repeatedly elevated results on a

57
00:03:24,463 --> 00:03:27,443
test used to screen for prostate cancer.

58
00:03:28,016 --> 00:03:31,366
Conventional tests approved by regulators later

59
00:03:31,366 --> 00:03:34,004
showed those results were inaccurate.

60
00:03:34,583 --> 00:03:38,574
Pregnant women received wrong pregnancy-hormone results.

61
00:03:38,574 --> 00:03:41,424
One was told she was likely miscarrying.

62
00:03:41,424 --> 00:03:44,631
Conventional tests showed a viable pregnancy.

63
00:03:45,116 --> 00:03:50,210
A Theranos employee on blood thinners got results far from earlier tests.

64
00:03:50,210 --> 00:03:52,024
A doctor changed the dose.

65
00:03:52,024 --> 00:03:55,932
A traditional lab later showed the change wasn't needed.

66
00:03:56,416 --> 00:04:01,230
The court says evidence linked Balwani to sending out those inaccurate

67
00:04:01,230 --> 00:04:06,182
results, and to buying adverts for Theranos wellness centres in Arizona.

68
00:04:06,750 --> 00:04:13,316
In the end, prosecutors say, Theranos itself concluded a patient impact existed for every

69
00:04:13,316 --> 00:04:18,260
test run on a patient, and it voided all tests run on its analyser.

70
00:04:18,850 --> 00:04:22,475
The trial judge found that decision was not voluntary.

71
00:04:22,475 --> 00:04:25,496
The appeals court let that stand, and said at

72
00:04:25,496 --> 00:04:28,382
Holmes's trial it could show what she knew.

73
00:04:28,950 --> 00:04:31,666
Patient health, the US Attorney said, is

74
00:04:31,666 --> 00:04:34,790
the highest priority of our healthcare system.

75
00:04:34,790 --> 00:04:37,914
And of Balwani, she said: he chose deceit over

76
00:04:37,914 --> 00:04:41,038
candour with patients in need of medical care.

77
00:04:41,683 --> 00:04:42,584
Chapter four.

78
00:04:42,584 --> 00:04:43,278
The pitch.

79
00:04:43,278 --> 00:04:45,843
Why did so much money keep coming in?

80
00:04:46,350 --> 00:04:51,624
By March 2015, prosecutors say, Theranos had raised more than seven

81
00:04:51,624 --> 00:04:56,191
hundred and thirty million dollars in its Series C rounds.

82
00:04:56,783 --> 00:05:01,124
The court says Theranos had no revenue in 2012 or

83
00:05:01,124 --> 00:05:07,148
2013, and lost fifty-seven million, then ninety-two million dollars.

84
00:05:07,750 --> 00:05:12,009
In November 2013, Balwani told Holmes the company

85
00:05:12,009 --> 00:05:15,833
was down to fifteen million dollars in cash.

86
00:05:16,416 --> 00:05:22,502
Yet at Holmes's trial, one investor testified she was shown a projected profit

87
00:05:22,502 --> 00:05:27,261
of two hundred and thirty million dollars by the end of 2015.

88
00:05:27,850 --> 00:05:32,674
Investors were also led to believe the military used the device.

89
00:05:32,674 --> 00:05:38,026
At Holmes's trial, General James Mattis testified it was never fielded.

90
00:05:38,516 --> 00:05:44,021
And reports carried the logos of drug companies that, their representatives said,

91
00:05:44,021 --> 00:05:48,710
had never validated the technology or allowed their logos to be used.

92
00:05:49,283 --> 00:05:51,941
In the court's words, Holmes and Balwani

93
00:05:51,941 --> 00:05:54,998
painted a very different picture to investors.

94
00:05:55,550 --> 00:06:00,344
Prosecutors say Balwani reviewed and approved a 2013 Wall Street

95
00:06:00,344 --> 00:06:05,812
Journal article calling the technology faster, cheaper and more accurate.

96
00:06:05,812 --> 00:06:08,659
They called that false and misleading.

97
00:06:09,250 --> 00:06:13,901
They also say the pair claimed Walgreens wellness centres would grow from

98
00:06:13,901 --> 00:06:18,679
a few dozen to nine hundred, while knowing the relationship was stagnating.

99
00:06:19,250 --> 00:06:24,757
The Securities and Exchange Commission also charged Balwani in 2018.

100
00:06:24,757 --> 00:06:29,212
Those are allegations; he chose to fight them in court.

101
00:06:29,716 --> 00:06:30,700
Chapter five.

102
00:06:30,700 --> 00:06:31,532
Two trials.

103
00:06:31,532 --> 00:06:33,424
Same judge, same company.

104
00:06:33,424 --> 00:06:35,391
So why different verdicts?

105
00:06:35,883 --> 00:06:40,880
Holmes and Balwani were tried separately, both before Judge Edward Davila.

106
00:06:40,880 --> 00:06:43,987
The trials were split after Holmes accused him

107
00:06:43,987 --> 00:06:47,229
of abuse in their relationship, which he denied.

108
00:06:47,783 --> 00:06:54,103
In January 2022, Holmes's jury convicted her on four investor counts, acquitted

109
00:06:54,103 --> 00:06:58,583
her on all four patient charges, and hung on three more.

110
00:06:59,150 --> 00:07:02,529
One clear difference: Holmes took the stand.

111
00:07:02,529 --> 00:07:03,758
Balwani did not.

112
00:07:04,250 --> 00:07:09,348
His lawyer reminded jurors that silence was his constitutional right.

113
00:07:09,850 --> 00:07:13,046
The government called about two dozen witnesses:

114
00:07:13,046 --> 00:07:17,041
patients, investors, former employees and business partners.

115
00:07:17,041 --> 00:07:18,572
The defence called two.

116
00:07:19,150 --> 00:07:24,398
ABC's Rebecca Jarvis called it the biggest difference between the trials.

117
00:07:24,883 --> 00:07:28,603
His defence leaned on missing evidence: a database

118
00:07:28,603 --> 00:07:31,505
of test results that no longer existed.

119
00:07:31,505 --> 00:07:37,160
In a scientific fraud case, his lawyer argued, you need the scientific data.

120
00:07:37,750 --> 00:07:43,446
The prosecutor called that speculation, and told jurors Balwani was no victim.

121
00:07:43,950 --> 00:07:47,406
Closing arguments alone took nearly four days.

122
00:07:47,916 --> 00:07:52,616
On the seventh of July 2022, after a four-month trial, the

123
00:07:52,616 --> 00:07:58,288
jury convicted him on all twelve counts, investors and patients alike.

124
00:07:58,883 --> 00:08:03,448
A verdict gives no reasons, so we won't guess what either jury thought.

125
00:08:03,950 --> 00:08:09,105
In December, Judge Davila sentenced him to a hundred and fifty-five months.

126
00:08:09,105 --> 00:08:12,611
Twelve years and eleven months, longer than Holmes.

127
00:08:13,116 --> 00:08:16,796
In May 2023, the court ordered the two of them,

128
00:08:16,796 --> 00:08:21,571
jointly, to repay four hundred and fifty-two million dollars.

129
00:08:22,150 --> 00:08:25,851
Prosecutors had asked for about eight hundred million.

130
00:08:25,851 --> 00:08:28,867
Both defendants, AP reported, said they were

131
00:08:28,867 --> 00:08:31,404
nearly broke after their legal bills.

132
00:08:31,983 --> 00:08:32,798
Chapter six.

133
00:08:32,798 --> 00:08:34,156
The false testimony.

134
00:08:34,156 --> 00:08:37,551
If a witness got it wrong, why didn't that matter?

135
00:08:38,050 --> 00:08:42,592
An investor witness, Bryan Tolbert, testified that Holmes said

136
00:08:42,592 --> 00:08:46,915
Theranos devices were used on military medevac helicopters.

137
00:08:47,483 --> 00:08:51,645
The appeals court accepted that statement was actually false.

138
00:08:51,645 --> 00:08:55,398
On that point, it said, Balwani is technically correct.

139
00:08:55,883 --> 00:08:59,993
Prosecutors have a duty not to let false testimony stand.

140
00:08:59,993 --> 00:09:04,608
The court assumed, without deciding, that the duty applied here.

141
00:09:05,116 --> 00:09:07,078
Here's the sentence we promised.

142
00:09:07,078 --> 00:09:11,676
Because he didn't raise this objection at trial, the court reviewed it only

143
00:09:11,676 --> 00:09:15,722
for plain error, and found it did not seriously affect his rights.

144
00:09:16,283 --> 00:09:21,486
At least two other witnesses, the court said, gave similar testimony.

145
00:09:21,486 --> 00:09:27,141
And Balwani never used the recording of the 2013 call to challenge Tolbert.

146
00:09:27,649 --> 00:09:30,798
The court also found some lab directors gave

147
00:09:30,798 --> 00:09:34,446
expert opinions without being qualified as experts.

148
00:09:34,446 --> 00:09:35,734
Harmless, it said.

149
00:09:35,734 --> 00:09:38,095
They would have qualified anyway.

150
00:09:38,683 --> 00:09:43,104
In December 2025, it refused to rehear the case.

151
00:09:43,104 --> 00:09:46,512
No judge asked for a full-court vote.

152
00:09:47,016 --> 00:09:50,251
His lawyers took both points to the Supreme Court.

153
00:09:50,251 --> 00:09:53,032
The government waived its right to respond.

154
00:09:53,516 --> 00:09:57,047
On the fifth of October 2026, the petition

155
00:09:57,047 --> 00:10:00,579
was denied, without a word of explanation.

156
00:10:01,149 --> 00:10:02,042
Our analysis.

157
00:10:02,042 --> 00:10:04,926
So why did the case against the number two

158
00:10:04,926 --> 00:10:08,633
hold where the case against the founder partly failed?

159
00:10:09,216 --> 00:10:11,646
This is our reading, not the court's.

160
00:10:11,646 --> 00:10:14,339
The patient case was about a lab, and the

161
00:10:14,339 --> 00:10:17,492
court record puts Balwani in charge of that lab.

162
00:10:18,050 --> 00:10:20,180
Holmes told her side for days.

163
00:10:20,180 --> 00:10:23,020
Balwani's jury heard no answer from him.

164
00:10:23,516 --> 00:10:24,961
And the false testimony?

165
00:10:24,961 --> 00:10:27,911
The courts didn't say it was harmless to tell it.

166
00:10:27,911 --> 00:10:31,644
They said it didn't change the outcome, given everything else.

167
00:10:32,150 --> 00:10:32,760
Who paid?

168
00:10:32,760 --> 00:10:35,609
Investors, who were owed three hundred and

169
00:10:35,609 --> 00:10:38,865
ninety-seven million dollars of the restitution.

170
00:10:38,865 --> 00:10:40,357
Walgreens and Safeway.

171
00:10:40,357 --> 00:10:45,308
And patients who were handed numbers they trusted about their own bodies.

172
00:10:45,883 --> 00:10:49,758
Our verdict: Balwani was not a sidekick in this record.

173
00:10:49,758 --> 00:10:52,859
He was the person the paperwork kept naming.

174
00:10:53,416 --> 00:10:55,860
For the founder's side of this story,

175
00:10:55,860 --> 00:10:58,833
watch our Theranos episode, linked on screen.

176
00:10:59,383 --> 00:11:01,224
Next Saturday: Thomas Cook.

177
00:11:01,224 --> 00:11:03,951
The world's oldest travel firm collapsed

178
00:11:03,951 --> 00:11:07,291
overnight, leaving holidaymakers stranded abroad.

179
00:11:07,291 --> 00:11:09,064
Who paid to fly them home?

180
00:11:09,616 --> 00:11:12,817
Every fact here is sourced in the description.

181
00:11:12,817 --> 00:11:15,739
Subscribe so the next case file finds you.
